\appendix
\section{Exploratory pooled cross-fitting}\label{app:crossfit}
For datasets with fewer than 460 calibration examples, an exploratory procedure augments the calibration loss matrix with fold-derived losses from the fit set. Five-fold models refit the standardizer and ridge heads, recompute ordering within each fold, and keep the deployed checkpoint unit counts. MiniRocket transform parameters remain fitted on the complete fit set. Stratified folds are used when each class has at least five examples; otherwise ordinary shuffled folds are used. Each held-out fold supplies disagreement with its own fold-specific full head, and these losses are pooled with those of the deployed model on the independent calibration set. The deployed model itself remains unchanged.

Pooling produced more finite thresholds and lower modeled cost (Table~\ref{tab:crossfit}). Its fold predictors differ from the deployed predictor, losses across folds are dependent, and transform parameters are shared. The split LTT and CRC arguments therefore do not apply to the pooled losses. This heuristic has no proved risk bound and differs from the construction analyzed by CV-CRC \cite{cvcrc}; the table reports its empirical operating points.

@@CROSSFIT@@

\section{Reproducibility}\label{app:repro}
The frozen baseline protocol identifier is retained in the accompanying evidence manifest. It records official source commits for Detach-ROCKET and POCKET, package versions, the operation-cost convention, candidate budgets, fit-only tuning and independent calibration. The manuscript tables are generated from the frozen aggregate results and the per-run ordering/cross-fitting files. The dataset manifest lists the 113 included datasets with fit, calibration and test sizes and sequence lengths.

